---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SectionHeader from "@/components/SectionHeader.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="BYOAg — Bring Your Own Agent"
  description="Explore BYOAg, an experimental open pattern for agent-portable experiences."
>
  <section
    class="relative overflow-hidden border-b border-white/10 bg-[#07111f]"
  >
    <div class="absolute inset-0 opacity-60" aria-hidden="true">
      <div
        class="h-full w-full bg-[radial-gradient(circle_at_70%_20%,rgba(56,189,248,0.16),transparent_28%),linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(245,158,11,0.12),transparent_38%)]"
      >
      </div>
    </div>
    <div
      class="page-shell relative grid min-h-[calc(100vh-65px)] items-center gap-10 py-20 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_440px]"
    >
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">
          Experimental open pattern for agent-portable experiences
        </p>
        <h1
          class="mt-5 max-w-4xl text-5xl font-black leading-[0.98] text-paper sm:text-6xl lg:text-7xl"
        >
          Bring your agent.<br />Enter the experience.<br />Do the work.
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-7 max-w-2xl text-xl leading-8 text-paper/76">
          BYOAg allows people to bring their own AI agent into an external
          environment where the experience provides the context, artifacts,
          tools, rules, and interaction contract.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-9 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
          <a
            class="rounded-md bg-accent px-5 py-3 font-bold text-ink transition hover:bg-accent/90"
            href="/concept"
          >
            Explore the concept
          </a>
          <a
            class="rounded-md border border-white/18 px-5 py-3 font-bold text-paper transition hover:border-cyan hover:bg-white/[0.06]"
            href="/how-it-works"
          >
            See how it works
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div
        class="rounded-lg border border-white/12 bg-white/[0.045] p-5 shadow-line"
      >
        <div class="grid gap-3 text-sm">
          <div class="rounded-md border border-white/10 bg-[#050c17] p-4">
            <p class="font-semibold text-paper">User-owned agent</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-paper/58">
              Carries continuity, preferences, and working style.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="mx-auto h-8 w-px bg-cyan/70" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <div class="rounded-md border border-accent/45 bg-accent/10 p-4">
            <p class="font-semibold text-paper">BYOAg entry point</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-paper/62">
              Publishes context, rules, artifacts, tools, and a contract.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="mx-auto h-8 w-px bg-cyan/70" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3">
            <span
              class="rounded-md border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.035] p-3 text-paper/78"
              >Submission</span
            >
            <span
              class="rounded-md border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.035] p-3 text-paper/78"
              >Feedback</span
            >
            <span
              class="rounded-md border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.035] p-3 text-paper/78"
              >Evidence</span
            >
            <span
              class="rounded-md border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.035] p-3 text-paper/78"
              >Continuation</span
            >
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-paper py-14 text-ink">
    <div
      class="page-shell grid gap-6 text-xl font-semibold leading-8 md:grid-cols-2"
    >
      <p>
        Traditional AI integrations bring data, tools, and context into an
        agent-controlled environment.
      </p>
      <p>
        BYOAg allows an agent to enter an environment-controlled experience.
        <span class="mt-4 block text-ink/70"
          >The agent remains the user's agent. The environment defines the work.</span
        >
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-[#07111f] py-24">
    <div class="page-shell">
      <SectionHeader
        eyebrow="The core model"
        title="Four roles, one interaction contract"
        text="BYOAg separates who brings intelligence from who defines the experience, artifacts, and rules."
      />
      <div
        class="mt-12 grid gap-4 lg:grid-cols-4"
        aria-label="BYOAg core model flow"
      >
        {
          [
            "Human",
            "Personal agent",
            "BYOAg environment",
            "Artifacts, tools, rules, and contracts",
          ].map((label, index) => (
            <div class="relative rounded-lg border border-white/12 bg-white/[0.04] p-5">
              <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-accent">0{index + 1}</p>
              <h3 class="mt-3 text-xl font-bold text-paper">{label}</h3>
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-paper/64">
                {
                  [
                    "Chooses the agent and authorizes the work.",
                    "Interprets the package and assists the user.",
                    "Publishes the work surface and evaluates results.",
                    "Constrain, explain, and record the interaction.",
                  ][index]
                }
              </p>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-[#0b1626] py-24">
    <div class="page-shell grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[360px_1fr]">
      <SectionHeader
        eyebrow="How it works"
        title="A small lifecycle for agent entry"
      />
      <ol class="grid gap-4">
        {
          [
            "The environment publishes an entry point.",
            "The user gives the entry point to their agent.",
            "The agent retrieves a Prompt Package or Agentic Contract.",
            "The agent performs the work and submits a result, receives feedback, or continues to the next interaction.",
          ].map((step, index) => (
            <li class="flex gap-4 rounded-lg border border-white/12 bg-white/[0.04] p-5">
              <span class="grid h-10 w-10 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-md bg-cyan/14 font-bold text-cyan">
                {index + 1}
              </span>
              <span class="pt-2 text-lg leading-7 text-paper/82">{step}</span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-paper py-24 text-ink">
    <div class="page-shell">
      <SectionHeader
        eyebrow="Why BYOAg"
        title="A pattern for shared work without forced agent ownership"
        text="The goal is not to guarantee perfect interoperability. It is to make the work surface explicit enough for different capable agents to participate."
      />
      <div class="mt-10 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
        {
          [
            "Users retain continuity with their preferred agent.",
            "Experiences do not need to own all intelligence.",
            "Environments can define consistent rules and evaluation criteria.",
            "Interactions can generate evidence of what was requested, attempted, and submitted.",
            "The same environment can work with different capable agents.",
          ].map((benefit) => (
            <p class="rounded-lg border border-ink/12 bg-white p-5 font-medium leading-7 text-ink/78">
              {benefit}
            </p>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-[#07111f] py-24">
    <div class="page-shell">
      <SectionHeader
        eyebrow="Initial use cases"
        title="Places where the pattern can be explored first"
      />
      <div class="mt-10 grid gap-5 lg:grid-cols-3">
        {
          [
            [
              "Education",
              "An environment provides activities, resources, constraints, and evaluation criteria. A student's agent helps them complete the activity, while an instructor's agent can evaluate submissions using a shared contract.",
            ],
            [
              "Games and interactive experiences",
              "An agent enters a game, trivia session, simulation, or branching story. Each submission can produce feedback, scoring, or the next scene.",
            ],
            [
              "Guided workflows",
              "An environment provides structured forms, procedures, artifacts, and checkpoints while the user's agent helps them navigate the process.",
            ],
          ].map(([title, text]) => (
            <article class="rounded-lg border border-white/12 bg-white/[0.04] p-6">
              <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-paper">{title}</h3>
              <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-paper/70">{text}</p>
            </article>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-[#fff8ed] py-20 text-ink">
    <div
      class="page-shell grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[0.9fr_1.1fr] lg:items-center"
    >
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Experimental status</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-black leading-tight">
          BYOAg is currently an experimental pattern.
        </h2>
      </div>
      <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-ink/72">
        It is being developed through prototypes, working examples,
        architectural discussion, and an evolving draft specification.
        Developers, researchers, product designers, educators, and agent
        builders are invited to explore, question, and contribute.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-[#0b1626] py-20">
    <div
      class="page-shell grid gap-8 rounded-lg border border-white/12 bg-white/[0.04] p-8 lg:grid-cols-[0.9fr_1.1fr] lg:items-center lg:p-10"
    >
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Design partners</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-black leading-tight text-paper">
          Exploring BYOAg for your organization?
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-paper/72">
          We are looking for early design partners interested in exploring
          agent-portable experiences, guided workflows, education, games,
          enterprise processes, and asynchronous agent interactions.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-paper/64">
          BYOAg is an open architectural pattern. Organizations may still need
          support identifying suitable use cases, designing interaction
          contracts, implementing secure integrations, and validating
          compatibility.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-7 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4">
          <!-- TODO: Replace with a public contact destination when one is configured. -->
          <button
            class="cursor-not-allowed rounded-md bg-accent px-5 py-3 font-bold text-ink/70 opacity-70"
            type="button"
            disabled
            title="A public contact destination is being arranged."
          >
            Discuss an implementation
          </button>
          <a
            class="font-semibold text-cyan underline hover:text-paper"
            href="/patterns"
          >
            Explore the patterns
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
